		<r3d:repositoryName language="eng">West of Scotland Twenty-07 Study</r3d:repositoryName>
				<r3d:repositoryUrl>http://2007study.sphsu.mrc.ac.uk/</r3d:repositoryUrl>
				<r3d:description language="eng">The Twenty-07 Study was set up in 1986 in order to investigate the reasons for differences in health by socio-economic circumstances, gender, area of residence, age, ethnic group, and family type.

4510 people are being followed for 20 years. The initial wave of data collection took place in 1987/8, when respondents were aged 15, 35 and 55. The final wave of data collection took place in 2007/08 when respondents were aged 35, 55 and 75.

In this way the Twenty-07 Study provides us with unique opportunities to investigate both the changes in people&#039;s lives over 20 years and how they affect their health, and the differences in people&#039;s experiences at the same ages 20 years apart, and how these have different effects on their health.</r3d:description>
